Z||000005||theogre||11-15-1999||10:34 PM||||Unless it's a plug or wire, a DIS motor generally won't skip on just one cyl from an ignition problem. If a coil is that bad it usually skips 2 cyls.<P>DXR,,, are you sure you don't have an exhaust leak expanding open when hot. These 4 cyls are great for craking manifolds. Especially the 86.5 up ones that have only one mount for the tranny.<P>In pat's case, if it's constant on 4 after all he's done, and he's sure it was done right with no leaks/cracks anyplace, then it sounds allot like a top ring is weak. Pat did you check the intake really well while it was off? If it's cracked you could be lean on one cyl.<BR>||||reg||1
